# Site (React + Vite)

Follow the **existing** structure. Keep code readable, maintainable, and reusable.

## File naming

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Routes, hooks, services, validators, store, **components**, **constants** | **kebab-case** | `public-routes.tsx`, `admin-login-form.tsx`, `mock-delays.ts` |
| Pages | **kebab-case** | `login.tsx`, `request-access.tsx` |
| Folders | **kebab-case** | `components/auth/`, `pages/public/` |

Component and page **filenames** use kebab-case; exported React symbols stay **PascalCase** (e.g. `admin-login-form.tsx` exports `AdminLoginForm`).

## Source layout (required)

```
site/src/
├── components/              # reusable UI — shared across pages/modules
│   └── {module}/            # feature module (auth, dashboard, …)
│       ├── {feature}.tsx    # composed module component (kebab-case file)
│       └── ui/              # small pieces used only inside this module
│           └── {piece}.tsx
├── hooks/                   # React Hook Form + UI operation logic
├── store/                   # Zustand stores (state + orchestration)
├── services/                # pure API call functions (no React)
├── validators/              # Zod schemas + inferred types
├── types/                   # shared interfaces & domain types (kebab-case per domain)
├── constants/               # static values: routes, limits, durations, formatting
├── config/                  # app wiring: nav menus, role-based redirect helpers
├── routes/
│   ├── main-router.tsx      # composes all route groups
│   ├── public-routes.tsx    # unauthenticated / marketing pages
│   ├── auth-routes.tsx      # login, register, verify, …
│   └── permitted-routes.tsx # RBAC-protected routes
├── pages/                   # route-level screens (thin — compose components)
│   ├── public/
│   ├── auth/
│   └── …
└── main.tsx
```

- New code goes in the correct layer. Do not put API calls in components or pages.
- Shared widgets used by 2+ modules → `components/` (not duplicated per module).
- Module-only small UI → `components/{module}/ui/`.

## Layer responsibilities

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| **pages/** | Route screens; compose `components/`; minimal logic |
| **components/** | Presentational & composed UI; props in, callbacks out |
| **components/{module}/ui/** | Tiny building blocks for one module only |
| **hooks/** | RHF setup (`useForm`, resolvers, submit handlers); no direct `fetch` |
| **store/** | Zustand slices; call `services/`; expose actions/selectors |
| **services/** | HTTP/API functions only; return typed data; no React imports |
| **validators/** | Zod schemas; export `z.infer<typeof Schema>` types |
| **types/** | Shared interfaces, API payloads/responses, domain models — not in services/config/utils |
| **constants/** | Static values and formatters: route paths, file limits, mock delays, locales, templates |
| **config/** | Nav definitions and role-based redirect logic (imports from `constants/` where needed) |
| **routes/** | `RouteObject[]` per access level; wire in `main-router.tsx` |

## UI vs logic

```tsx
// BAD — API + form state inside a page/component
const Login = () => {
  const onSubmit = async () => { await fetch('/api/login', …); };
};

// GOOD — thin page, hook for RHF, store/service for API
const Login = () => <LoginForm {...useLoginForm()} />;
```

- **Forms: React Hook Form** (`react-hook-form`) + Zod resolver (`@hookform/resolvers/zod`).
- **State: Zustand** — global/session state and async orchestration via store actions.
- **Validation: Zod** — schemas live in `validators/`; reuse in hooks and services.

## Routing & RBAC

- **`public-routes.tsx`** — no auth required (home, about, …).
- **`auth-routes.tsx`** — sign-in flow; redirect if already authenticated.
- **`permitted-routes.tsx`** — protected routes; enforce role/permission before render.
- Register all groups in `main-router.tsx`; do not scatter route definitions in pages.

## Dependencies

Add via `package.json` when introducing each concern — do not invent a second solution:

- `react-hook-form`, `@hookform/resolvers` — forms
- `zustand` — client state
- `zod` — validation
- API client (e.g. `axios` or shared `fetch` wrapper) in `services/`
- `shadcn/ui` (radix base) — generated primitives in `src/components/ui/`, imported via
  the `@/*` alias. That directory belongs to the shadcn CLI and is **not** the same as
  `components/{module}/ui/` (module-local pieces). Add with
  `cmd.exe /c "cd /d C:\DE4RD\cares-infra\site && pnpm dlx shadcn@latest add <name> --yes"`.
  Its theme tokens alias onto the `--cares-*` palette in `index.css` — never give a
  shadcn token its own literal colour, and no `dark:` classes (the portal is light-only).

## Loading states

- First load of a known layout → a `*-skeleton.tsx` mirror built from the `Skeleton`
  primitive, placed beside the component it mirrors in `components/{module}/ui/`
  (portal-wide ones in `components/portal/ui/`). No hand-rolled `animate-pulse` divs.
- Refetch/pagination keeps the existing data on screen; gate the skeleton on first load
  (`loading && items.length === 0`). User-initiated actions get an in-button spinner.
- Skeleton dimensions and counts come from the same constants/props as the real
  component so the swap causes no layout jump.
- Gate redirects on `auth-store`'s `initialized`, rendering a skeleton while
  `checkAuth()` is in flight.

## Environment

- Use **`.env`** / `import.meta.env` for API base URL and public config.
- Never hardcode secrets, tokens, or API keys in source.

## Quality bar

- Keep pages and composed components **under ~300 lines**; split into `ui/` or hooks.
- Prefer composition over copy-paste; extract repeated UI to `components/`.
- Types from Zod (`z.infer`) live in `validators/`; explicit shared interfaces live in `types/` (group by domain, kebab-case filenames). Component-local `*Props` may stay in the component file. Avoid `any`.
- Static literals (route paths, timeouts, file-size limits, locale strings, email templates) and shared formatting helpers live in `constants/` (kebab-case per domain). Do not scatter magic numbers or inline `Intl`/`dayjs` formatters in pages or components.
